# interplay_lifetime_one_reference_two_kinds: The object manager keeps one map per kind, and a reference names an object in each. A delete of the wrong kind forgets nothing: 40 with operation 1006 (a compute pipeline) on a buffer's reference, and 37 on a pipeline's, leave both live. And one reference can hold two live objects at once: a buffer, cached, whose entry the guest then rewrites into a compute pipeline's record (type 7) is made a pipeline by the next dispatch, while the next blit still finds the buffer; a 37 then drops the buffer and the next blit tries to make one from the pipeline's record, which fails ("Failed to create Buffer"), while the pipeline, in its own map, still dispatches.
